Few characters ago my chaotic orc ranger managed to summon Juiblex.
Nice to meet a peaceful demon prince, but... what good is it? It is
just there. Does it guarantee I will never have to fight that
particular demon?

Now I am playing Cha-Elf-Wiz-Fem named Lethe, and she is at XL 13 -
highest I ever got. The deepest I ever got was to DL 20-22 or so with a
monk, but the monk XL never got past 12. My usual strategy is to clean
out Gnomish Mines first, but Lethe had a sucky AC for a long time, so I
retreated from Mines DL 9 after expending a scare monster scroll on
some fire ants. Lethe cleaned out Sokoban, got amulet of reflection,
reached DL 11, found a chaotic altar at DL 9, and sacrificed a unicorn
- my first time ever! At XL 12 she went back to Minetown - still with
only two pieces of armor (cloak and helmet) and AC 4!

Now Lethe bought up whatever was left to buy at Minetown, polymorphed
Watch Captain into a wraith - hence XL 13 and (finally!) some gloves
and non-metal boots. She is Expert with her +4 staff, has teleportitis
and ring of teleport control, and I am debating whether it is
worthwhile to go down to Gnome King cellar, or should I say good-buy to
the Mines now?

BTW, Lethe acquired her ring of teleport control (probably the most
useful possession so far) by polymorphing another ring. She already had
teleportitis, and I badly needed that particular ring, and got it - on
the first try. Likewise, when Lethe polymorphed the Watch Captain, it
was hard to come up with a better outcome. Was that pure (i.e.
non-coded) luck, or is the program smart enough to figure out what your
character could really use, and to provide that if his Luck is high
enough?

Lethe's biggest problem now, IMO, is lack of low-level spells other
than attack and enchantment schools. She already knows 9 or 10 spells,
but only uses force bolt, sleep, magic missile and protection. All her
other spells have failure rates in 90-100% range, so I don't even
bother.



